# Rule 2, GHC's rule for overlapping instances: a call at a value of
# parameter type to an overload set whose candidates are separated by a
# concept resolves, at each instantiation, by whether that concept holds; if
# the enclosing template's constraints neither require nor negate it, the
# body varies with the type through a constraint it did not declare, and the
# translation into System F (which resolves at the type variable) and the
# compiler (which resolves at the instantiation) disagree.  Decide it in the
# clause, by requiring the concept or by splitting on it.  A call the
# constraints name is read through the dictionary and is not judged.
tool undecided-resolution
